{
    "title": "Linear Dependence in 2D",
    "pathToSources": "Courses/MathForComputerGraphics/Chapter 2/Block 2/",
    "steps": [
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Welcome! Today, we’ll explore dependent vectors.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Let's try to use our words to describe important properties.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Flashcards",
            "flashcards": [
                {
                    "frontText": "Vectors u and v are linearly dependent if…",
                    "backText": "…there exists a number α ∈ ℝ \\ {0} such that v = αu."
                },
                {
                    "frontText": "Are two vectors independent if they are not dependent?",
                    "backText": "Yes"
                },
                {
                    "frontText": "What does it mean if some vectors are dependent?",
                    "backText": "It means we can build one of them by mixing (linear combination) the others."
                },
                {
                    "frontText": "A set of vectors is independent if…",
                    "backText": "…the only linear combination that gives the zero vector is when all the coefficients are zero."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Let’s determine whether two vectors are dependent: u = (2,1) and v = (4,2). Can we find a number α such that v = αu?",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "multipleChoice": {
                "answers": [
                    {
                        "text": "α = 1",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "α = 2",
                        "isCorrect": true,
                        "feedback": "Exactly! v = 2u → linearly dependent."
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "α = 1/2",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "No such α",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Now let’s check geometrically:",
            "contentType": "Geometry",
            "interaction": "Continue",
            "geometry": {
                "isNewScene": true,
                "properties": {
                    "showGridLines": true,
                    "showAxes": true,
                    "showNumbers": true,
                    "gridBounds": {
                        "minX": -5,
                        "maxX": 5,
                        "minY": -2,
                        "maxY": 5
                    }
                },
                "geometryObjects": {
                    "Add": [
                        {
                            "id": "u",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    1
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    2,
                                    2
                                ],
                                "label": "u"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "v",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    4,
                                    2
                                ],
                                "label": "v"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "There was a quick way to tell if vectors are linearly dependent. What was it?",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "multipleChoice": {
                "answers": [
                    {
                        "text": "same length",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "perpendicularity",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "parallelism",
                        "isCorrect": true,
                        "feedback": "Correct. But be careful — in higher dimensions, ‘parallel’ might not be all!"
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Perfect, and what about the set of these 5 vectors — is it linearly dependent?",
            "contentType": "Geometry",
            "interaction": "MultipleChoice",
            "geometry": {
                "isNewScene": true,
                "properties": {
                    "showGridLines": true,
                    "showAxes": true,
                    "showNumbers": true,
                    "gridBounds": {
                        "minX": -4,
                        "maxX": 4,
                        "minY": -3,
                        "maxY": 3
                    }
                },
                "geometryObjects": {
                    "Add": [
                        {
                            "id": "vec1",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    1,
                                    2
                                ],
                                "label": "a"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "vec2",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    2,
                                    1
                                ],
                                "label": "b"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "vec3",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    -1,
                                    3
                                ],
                                "label": "c"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "vec4",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    3,
                                    -2
                                ],
                                "label": "d"
                            }
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "vec5",
                            "objectType": "Vector",
                            "vectorData": {
                                "start": [
                                    0,
                                    0
                                ],
                                "end": [
                                    -2,
                                    -1
                                ],
                                "label": "e"
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "multipleChoice": {
                "answers": [
                    {
                        "text": "yes",
                        "isCorrect": true
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "no",
                        "isCorrect": false
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "some of them",
                        "isCorrect": false,
                        "feedback": "Careful: linear (in)dependence is about the whole collection. Not only a pair."
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Ah, so for example, the vector b can be expressed as a linear combination of other vectors (e.g., c+d), so in a sense it is redundant.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Exactly, right!",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Is there a simple way to see if a set of vectors is linearly independent?",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Well, first of all, if you have more than 2 vectors in 2D, then there is always redundancy, so they are dependent.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue",
            "saveFact": true,
            "factData": {
                "text1": "Linearly Dependent Vectors in nD",
                "text2": "In nD, at most n linearly independent vectors can exist.",
                "speaker": "Assistant"
            }
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Assistant",
            "message": "Ah, and for 2 vectors we solve v = αu as above?",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "Exactly. In the next lecture, we’re going to take a look at how to do it in higher dimensions.",
            "contentType": "OnlyText",
            "interaction": "Continue"
        },
        {
            "speaker": "Teacher",
            "message": "But first let’s match some pairs:",
